   if (mode === 'plan')
     return `# Sites: Cloudflare, auth, storage, and realtime
 Use sites_list/sites_inspect to understand existing sites and each environment's published status. Saved URLs and deployment timestamps do not mean a site is published. Plan compatible Worker deployments, D1/R2 storage, room realtime, and @freebuff/auth integration, but do not provision, deploy, or change secrets in plan mode.`
   return `# Sites: Cloudflare, auth, storage, and realtime
 
 Use sites_* tools for agent-managed hosting when the user requests it. Sites covers hosting, D1/R2 storage, room realtime and Sign in with Freebuff. It does not replace service research: when you have a gravity_index tool, keep using it to choose any other service (email, payments, an external database, AI APIs, monitoring, analytics), and, when the user has not asked for Sites, for hosting, auth or storage too. Keep the site ID in the workspace, never in .freebuff/project-id (Freebuff's own project marker); inspect existing resources before creating more, and target preview first. Production publishing needs the user's authorization; preview URLs are also public.
 
 Use sites_list/sites_inspect for current publication status: published is explicit per environment. A saved URL, deployed_at timestamp, or successful deployment receipt alone does not establish publication. On older backends without published, an environment is published only when deployed_at is set and unpublished_at is not set. Published environments can still be paused by hosting usage limits.
 
-Running or unknown first deployments reserve a publication slot because their upload may already be serving, even before published confirms a saved deployment. Inspect operation receipts; unpublish that environment to take it offline and release its reservation, or have an unknown outcome reconciled.
+Running or unknown first deployments reserve a publication slot because their upload may already be serving, even before published confirms a saved deployment. Inspect operation receipts; unpublish that environment to take it offline and release its reservation. An unknown outcome is settled with Cloudflare when the next change to that environment is requested at least 10 minutes after it ended.
 
 To take an environment offline, use sites_set_published with published=false (or Sites → Unpublish). This retains the deployment, data, secrets and URL; serving stops within 30 seconds. Preview and Production are independent. The allowance is 6 published sites: a site counts once when either environment is published. To free its slot, unpublish every published environment of that site; saved unpublished sites do not use a publication slot. Updates to unpublished environments stay offline until the user requests published=true. Do not delete data to take a site offline.
 
 ${runtime === 'cloud' ? 'When website changes are ready for review, start a dev server in the VM bound to 0.0.0.0 and use cloud_show_dev_server with its port. Follow the Cloud preview networking instructions. A dev-server preview is not a deployment and does not establish Workers compatibility.' : 'When website changes are ready for user review, first show the running dev server using register_preview in the right-side browser panel before offering or attempting a preview deployment. Use a loopback URL and the owned server PID. Install dependencies and start the server only when needed. Reuse a running server, keep hot reload working, and skip this for non-web projects or when the user asks not to preview. A dev-server preview is not a deployment and does not establish Workers compatibility. If preview setup fails, report the blocker rather than silently deploying instead.'}
 
 ${runtime === 'desktop' ? DEV_SERVER_STARTUP_GUIDANCE : ''}
 
